    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2+y^2-x-5y+4=0$.\n\nSubstitute the three points into the general form and solve for its coefficients.",
      "worked": "Substituting the three points gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n-2g+6f+c&=-10 &&\\text{from }(-1,3),\\qquad\\text{(1)}\\\\\n4g+4f+c&=-8 &&\\text{from }(2,2),\\qquad\\text{(2)}\\\\\n2g+8f+c&=-17 &&\\text{from }(1,4).\\qquad\\text{(3)}\n\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting (1) from (2), and (2) from (3), gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n6g-2f&=2,\\\\\n-2g+4f&=-9.\n\\end{align*}$$\nTwice the first equation plus the second gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\n10g&=-5,\\\\\ng&=-\\frac12.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{align*}\n-3-2f&=2,\\\\\nf&=-\\frac52,\\\\\n1-15+c&=-10,\\\\\nc&=4.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence the circle is $x^2+y^2-x-5y+4=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
